17:15.293 --> 17:17.023
you've developed a terrible attitude.

17:17.129 --> 17:20.395
And all the success with the family band
is only making it worse.

17:20.500 --> 17:22.127
The family band?

17:22.469 --> 17:26.237
You know, maybe you haven't noticed,
Lois, but I am the band.

17:26.341 --> 17:30.301
- Right, Missus Wong?
- Yeah, she band. Old lady jealous.

17:31.647 --> 17:34.481
Peter, we have to do something.
We're losing our daughter.

17:34.585 --> 17:36.349
I'm worried about
what's happening to her.

17:36.454 --> 17:37.944
Lois, this is the kind of thing...

17:38.056 --> 17:41.026
that always resolves itself
if you just ignore it, all right?

17:41.127 --> 17:43.688
What's more important is
we're living the sweet life.

17:43.797 --> 17:46.596
This is even more fun than
when I performed at the White House.

17:47.001 --> 17:49.971
Mr. President,
I present to you Peter Griffin.

18:05.559 --> 18:07.960
Okay, listen up, everybody.
I got great news.

18:08.196 --> 18:12.395
<i>Meg, you and your family are gonna
perform on Saturday Night Live.</i>

18:12.835 --> 18:15.771
You mean I'm gonna get to meet
John Belushi and Gilda Radner...

18:15.872 --> 18:19.001
and Phil Hartman, and Chris Farley,
and Horatio Sanz? Sweet!

18:23.450 --> 18:25.418
<i>Saturday Night Live.</i>

18:25.518 --> 18:28.215
I can't think of anything more exciting.

18:28.322 --> 18:31.087
Oh, my God, a water fountain!

18:34.197 --> 18:37.599
Meg, I'm Jimmy Fallon.

18:37.701 --> 18:40.762
It's great to finally meet you. I'm hosting.

18:41.974 --> 18:44.169
Why don't you come hang out
in my dressing room?

18:44.276 --> 18:46.211
- What are you looking at?
- Nothing.

18:46.313 --> 18:47.940
Come on, let's go.

18:48.216 --> 18:51.709
Peter, I'm worried about Meg.
She's spiraling out of control.

18:51.820 --> 18:53.947
I mean, what if she develops
a coke problem?

18:54.056 --> 18:55.547
No Coke. Pepsi.

18:56.893 --> 18:59.294
Come on, you set me up for that one.

19:03.301 --> 19:04.428
Wow, Jimmy.

19:04.537 --> 19:07.234
<i>That was everything
Ladies Home Journal said it would be.</i>

19:07.341 --> 19:09.206
Awesome, great, thanks.

19:10.110 --> 19:12.477
You know, there's something I...

19:12.814 --> 19:14.305
There's something I gotta tell you.

19:14.416 --> 19:17.614
Being with you just made me feel
so... Live from New York...

19:17.721 --> 19:19.621
<i>it's Saturday Night!</i>

19:20.958 --> 19:23.450
<i>It's Saturday Night Live.</i>

19:23.562 --> 19:25.029
Oh, my God.

19:25.130 --> 19:27.395
Yeah, that wasn't a very good
opening sketch, was it?

19:27.500 --> 19:30.629
- A rare miss.
- I don't think that was a sketch, Peter.

19:31.372 --> 19:34.342
Mom, Dad, he used me for comedy.

19:34.442 --> 19:35.568
Wait a minute.

19:35.678 --> 19:37.942
Are you telling me
that my daughter was deflowered...

19:38.047 --> 19:40.608
<i>in front of one-and-a-half times
the Mad TVaudience?</i>

19:40.717 --> 19:41.980
My poor baby.

19:42.086 --> 19:43.781
My God, Lois, you were right.

19:43.888 --> 19:45.754
Why the hell didn't I see it coming?

19:45.858 --> 19:49.989
All right, stand aside.
It's about time I did my fatherly duty.

19:50.697 --> 19:53.223
I said "duty," but no time
to laugh about it now.

19:55.504 --> 19:57.769
Hey, everybody, it's great to be back.

19:57.874 --> 19:59.842
So we got a great show tonight and...

19:59.943 --> 20:02.674
Hey, Fallon, say goodnight, you bum.

20:03.814 --> 20:06.079
And this is for laughing
and looking at the camera...

20:06.184 --> 20:07.743
during every sketch you've ever been in.

20:07.853 --> 20:09.878
Who do you think you are? Carol Burnett?

20:09.989 --> 20:12.925
You think because she did it,
it's okay for you?

20:13.026 --> 20:15.552
You haven't earned what she's earned,
buddy.

20:15.663 --> 20:17.962
All right, now where's the guy
who slept with my daughter?

20:20.270 --> 20:22.568
I'm so glad to be the real me again.

20:22.672 --> 20:24.766
It's too much work being beautiful.

20:24.875 --> 20:27.709
Not for me, but it's good
to have you back, pumpkin.

20:27.813 --> 20:30.476
Well, I guess there's only
one thing left to do.

20:35.222 --> 20:37.623
Listen, thanks, everybody.
I had a great time tonight.

20:37.726 --> 20:40.696
I want to thank Jimmy Fallon
for being such a good sport.

20:41.364 --> 20:45.564
Lois, Meg, Stewie, Brian, Chris,
the guys from the prison...

20:45.670 --> 20:47.160
Counting Crows.

20:47.505 --> 20:50.168
If I'm forgetting anybody, I'm sorry.
Goodnight, everybody!

20:50.275 --> 20:51.868
Our thoughts are with you, Chevy!

20:57.218 --> 21:00.245
<i>From the world famous
Apollo Theater in Harlem...</i>

21:00.355 --> 21:02.449
<i>it's show time at the...</i>

21:03.826 --> 21:05.385
What? I'm tired.

21:06.063 --> 21:08.897
It has nothing to do with the fact
that it's a black show.

21:09.000 --> 21:11.469
What? I can't be tired at 1:00
in the morning?

21:11.470 --> 22:12.470
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru